Z||000000||Feenx||12-15-2000||02:34 AM||||I have a question that has probly bin answered countless times on this Forum.<BR>but here goes..I have to replace my 2.5 motor <BR>in my 86 coupe.<BR>I've got another motor but will have remove it where it sits (the donor car), My question is .<BR>is it easier to pull the motor from above or from the bottom..<BR>any input to this would be a great help<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>86 Sport Coupe (Red)<BR>2.5l Auto||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||12-15-2000||09:54 AM||||<BR>I just replaced the 4-cyl in my 84 and I pulled it through the bottom.  I did not find it difficult, just tidious(sp).<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||12-16-2000||10:37 AM||||Good question. I replaced the motor in my '86 coupe about 7 months ago. I ended up pulling the motor out through the bottom of the car, and since it was getting a new shortblock (and I was too lazy to strip the motor down and pull it from the top) I ended up putting the motor back in (in a longblock state) through the top. All in all, I'd have to say replacement was MUCH easier than removal due to the fact that I had trouble raising the car enough for the cylinder head to clear from under it. <P>P.S. Due to recent complications with my engine I would HIGHLY suggest that even if it's getting a NEW motor, that you replace the timing gear with something a little stronger (steel or alluminum). Had my fiber gear break up on me with less than 10K miles, and having to replace it already, and it would have been MUCH easier to do it with the motor completely out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||William Federle||12-16-2000||12:54 PM||||I read in a post on this forum not too long ago that if the cradle and all that it carries is detatched from the rest of the car, that two people, one on each side can lift the rear of the car by hand and roll it forward away from the cradle etc. Has anyone ever actually done that?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-17-2000||07:18 PM||||ok.<BR>I also have removed engine from bottom.<BR>But i just bought an 88 and don't want to disturb the suspension any and would like to know if it is terribly harder to remove engine from top. <BR>Also put steel timing gears on and new oil pump.I was told to do so and later regretted not.||||reg||1
